'My proposed solution will utilize the powerful YOLOv8 segmentation model from the `ultralytics` library, which is well-suited for instance segmentation tasks. I will first convert the provided `CellSegDataset` into the YOLO format using the helper function available in the dataset class, creating separate training and validation splits. Then, I will fine-tune a large, pre-trained YOLOv8 model (`yolov8l-seg.pt`) on this formatted training data, leveraging the high-resolution capabilities of the model by setting the image size to 1024x1024 to preserve details of small cells. After training, the best model checkpoint will be used to perform inference on the validation images. Finally, I will process the model's output, combining the individual instance masks into a single final segmentation map with unique integer IDs for each cell as required. For evaluation, I will rely on the mean Average Precision (mAP) at an IoU threshold of 0.5 for segmentation masks, which is automatically calculated and logged by the YOLOv8 training framework on the validation set.'
